what's happening in this forgotten  province of Northwest Syria represents a  huge escalation a haze of smoke rising  from the grounds marking a fresh wave of  bombings Syrian regime forces emboldened  and protected by Russian air cover a  widening their offensive the area's  mostly help bite area and Shack formerly  known as the looser affront and once an  offshoot of al Qaeda last year a deal  between Russia and Turkey created a  demilitarized zone from which the  jihadists were meant to retreat but the  Kremlin claims that's not happened which  is why we're now seeing Moscow's war  machine kicking up a gear Damascus sees  this as an opportunity to recover more  territory  President Assad indicating he'll pay the  price in spilt blood to regain every  inch of Syrian soil the bodies of dead  militants lie in the areas that have now  been taken back and anyone who's  witnessed the brutality of the Assad  regime will not doubt it's intense  deadly barrel bombs have been dropped  over this area causing huge numbers to  flee  many of these people are already  refugees of the Syrian conflict and now  they're being displaced again we ran  away from bombing it's destroyed  everything we're sewing to make a  shelter under the trees we are six  families and don't have anywhere to go  and no one is helping us at least 50  villages have been under the shelling  and aerial bombardment  if the conflagration broadens the  consequences will be devastating for the  region's 3 million residents a million  of them are children  we condemn the last of innocent civilian  lives and we are alarmed by the  displacement of over 150 thousand  persons as well as the targeting of  population centers and civilian  infrastructure including hospitals and  schools this offensive may be limited at  the moment but the danger of escalation  is very real and would represent a major  challenge to the international community  the UN is trying to calm the fighting  through diplomatic channels but the  warnings have so far been ignored  Alex Rossi Sky News
 

